#  Core units gnatprove has not analyzed, and why each is still excused.
#
#  This file is the reason the proof-closure lint can stay ON.  An
#  unanalyzed core unit that is not listed here fails the lint; a waiver
#  naming a unit gnatprove HAS since analyzed is stale and fails too, so
#  the list cannot outlive what it excuses.
#
#  columns: unit  reason
fabula-numbers-real_text  decimal text to Long_Float ('Value) stays outside the proof by design: a correctly rounded conversion is out of scope; the spec is SPARK, the body SPARK_Mode Off; Parse_Real passes it only text that its proved grammar check accepted (-?[0-9]*\.?[0-9]+), and the body never raises: it catches Constraint_Error and tests 'Valid, so an overflow to infinity is Out_Of_Range
